   "source": [
    "# Phase 4 \u2014 Python / Pandas EDA",
    "**Dataset:** `ecommerce_sales_for_mysql.csv` (34,500 cleaned e-commerce order rows, 12 Sep 2023 \u2013 11 Sep 2025)",
    "",
    "This notebook continues from Phases 1\u20133 (Excel cleaning, Excel analysis, SQL analysis) and performs exploratory data analysis in Python/pandas.",
    "",
    "**Known constraints carried over from earlier phases (validated again below, not just assumed):**",
    "- `customer_id` and `product_id` behave as per-row labels, not stable entity keys \u2014 repeat IDs show conflicting age/region/gender or category. Customer/product-level analysis is treated as *pattern-only*, not ground truth.",
    "- `profit_margin` is a **currency amount**, not a percentage, despite the name. `profit_margin_pct = profit_margin / total_amount * 100` is computed fresh in this notebook.",
    "- 2023 and 2025 are **partial years** (coverage starts 2023\u201109\u201112, ends 2025\u201109\u201111) \u2014 raw annual totals are not compared without normalizing.",
    ""
   ]
  },
